From 872d5ff4b599b196ce165e1b0359d8d00587da0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Van Tran <trantoanvan@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:24:49 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(inbox): "Needs you" and "For your info" tabs

The active inbox shows one of two tabs. A row (an issue's notifications,
grouped) is in "Needs you" when any of its unarchived notifications is
marked above info by the server (action_required: assigned to you, a
decision to answer, a run that failed; attention: an autopilot problem)
and its issue is not done or closed; the rest is "For your info". The
grouped row shows only the newest notification, often a comment, so the
split reads every unarchived notification, not the row. It opens on
"Needs you" while that holds anything; that count is red. Each "Needs you"
row starts with a chip naming the notification that asks. Archive stays
"Done"; filters apply inside the tab. Web only. Reference: OpenMausBot's
Needs you / For your info / Done.

Patch-Id: inbox-split
